(     submit a written request to Provider's Notice Address within thirty \(30\)) Tj
T*
(     days after the end of the calendar month in which the Downtime occurred.) Tj
T*
(     The request must include: \(a\) the dates and times of the Downtime;) Tj
T*
(     \(b\) a description of how the Cloud Service was affected; and \(c\) any) Tj
T*
(     supporting evidence such as error logs or screenshots. Provider will) Tj
T*
(     review the request and, if it confirms that the Uptime Target was not) Tj
T*
(     met, will apply the Service Credit to Customer's next invoice.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3.3  Maximum Credit. The total Service Credits for any single calendar month) Tj
T*
(     will not exceed fifty percent \(50%\) of the Monthly Fee for that month.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3.4  Sole Remedy. Service Credits are Customer's sole and exclusive remedy) Tj
T*
(     for Provider's failure to meet the Uptime Target, except as otherwise) Tj
T*
(     provided in the Agreement.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SECTION 4 ? REPORTING) Tj
T*
(----------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4.1  Provider will make Monthly Uptime Percentage data available to Customer) Tj
T*
(     through the Provider's online dashboard or upon written request.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4.2  Provider will maintain service-availability logs for at least twelve) Tj
T*
(     \(12\) months and will make them available to Customer upon reasonable) Tj
T*
(     request for the purpose of verifying Service Credits.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SECTION 5 ? EXCLUSIONS) Tj
T*
(------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The following are excluded from the calculation of Downtime Minutes:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5.1  Scheduled Maintenance, as defined in Section 1.3.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5.2  Downtime caused by Customer's equipment, software, network connections,) Tj
T*
(     or other infrastructure not provided by Provider.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5.3  Downtime caused by Customer's use of the Cloud Service in a manner not) Tj
T*
(     authorized by the Agreement or the Documentation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5.4  Downtime caused by a Force Majeure Event as defined in the Standard Terms.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5.5  Downtime resulting from actions or inactions of third parties outside) Tj
T*
(     Provider's reasonable control, including internet service providers,) Tj
T*
(     DNS providers, and certificate authorities.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SECTION 6 ? TERMINATION FOR PERSISTENT FAILURES) Tj
T*
(-------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6.1  If the Monthly Uptime Percentage falls below the Uptime Target in any) Tj
T*
(     two \(2\) consecutive calendar months, Customer may, in addition to any) Tj
T*
(     Service Credits, terminate the Agreement upon thirty \(30\) days' written) Tj
T*
(     notice to Provider. In such event, Provider will refund to Customer a) Tj
T*
(     prorated portion of any prepaid Fees for the remainder of the) Tj
T*
(     Subscription Period.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(================================================================================) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This SLA is effective as of the Effective Date of the Agreement and will) Tj
T*
(remain in effect for the duration of the Agreement, including any renewal) Tj
T*
(periods.) Tj
